      <div style="font-size:12px; color:var(--muted);">Kaggle Banking Default Corpus</div>
    </div>

    <div class="metric-summary-card">
      <div style="font-size:11px; text-transform:uppercase; font-weight:700; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:6px;">Feature Dimensions</div>
      <div style="font-size:20px; font-weight:700; color:var(--text); margin-bottom:4px;">16 &rarr; 24 Columns</div>
      <div style="font-size:12px; color:var(--muted);">9 Continuous + 15 One-Hot Dummies</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Context Narrative Card -->
  <div class="card" style="padding:28px; margin-bottom:28px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:18px; font-weight:700; margin:0 0 12px;">Problem Statement & Business Objective</h2>
    <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--muted); line-height:1.7; margin:0 0 16px;">
      Financial lending institutions disburse tens of thousands of credit facilities annually. A non-negligible fraction of borrowers experience financial insolvency or delinquency, causing Non-Performing Assets (NPAs) and capital write-offs. The goal of this machine learning system is to classify whether an applicant presents an unacceptable probability of default prior to capital deployment.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--muted); line-height:1.7; margin:0;">
      Rather than relying purely on blunt bureau thresholds (e.g. FICO cutoffs), LoanLens evaluates a multivariate vector of borrower liquidity (DTI ratio, income), leverage (loan principal, interest burden), and stability (employment tenure, collateral, co-signer presence).
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Preprocessing & Partitioning Split -->
  <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:20px; margin-bottom:28px;">
    <div class="card" style="padding:24px;">
      <h3 style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin:0 0 14px;">Data Partitioning & Class Balance</h3>
      <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:12px; font-size:13px;">
        <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; padding-bottom:10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">
          <span style="color:var(--muted);">Training Partition (80%)</span>
          <span style="font-weight:600;">204,277 Applications</span>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; padding-bottom:10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">
          <span style="color:var(--muted);">Held-Out Test Partition (20%)</span>
          <span style="font-weight:600;">51,070 Applications</span>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; padding-bottom:10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">
          <span style="color:var(--muted);">Class Distribution</span>
          <span style="font-weight:600;">88.4% Non-Default / 11.6% Default</span>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between;">
          <span style="color:var(--muted);">Evaluation Scheme</span>
          <span style="font-weight:600; color:var(--brand);">5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="padding:24px;">
      <h3 style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin:0 0 14px;">Preprocessing & Transformation Protocol</h3>
      <ul style="margin:0; padding-left:18px; font-size:13px; color:var(--muted); line-height:1.7;">
        <li><strong>StandardScaler Normalization:</strong> Applied to all continuous numerical attributes (Age, Income, LoanAmount, CreditScore, MonthsEmployed, NumCreditLines, InterestRate, LoanTerm, DTIRatio) to guarantee zero mean ($\mu=0$) and unit variance ($\sigma=1$).</li>
        <li><strong>One-Hot Dummy Encoding:</strong> Categoricals (Education, EmploymentType, MaritalStatus, LoanPurpose, HasMortgage, HasDependents, HasCoSigner) encoded using <code>drop_first=True</code> to eliminate multicollinearity.</li>
        <li><strong>Identifier Pruning:</strong> Unique ID column <code>LoanID</code> dropped as non-predictive surrogate index.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SOP Requirement: Scratch Implementation Spotlight -->
  <div class="card" style="padding:24px; border-left:4px solid var(--brand); margin-bottom:28px;">
    <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:flex-start; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:12px; margin-bottom:10px;">
      <div>
        <span class="badge" style="background:rgba(2,132,199,0.15); color:#0284c7; margin-bottom:6px;">ML Project SOP Section 4 Compliance</span>
        <h3 style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin:0;">Scratch Algorithm Implementation: Logistic Regression via Gradient Descent</h3>
      </div>
      <span style="font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:var(--brand);">NumPy Only (Zero Scikit-Learn)</span>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--muted); line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 12px;">
      As mandated by the ML Project Standard Operating Procedure, at least one algorithm is implemented strictly from fundamental mathematics. The custom gradient descent optimizer minimizes the binary cross-entropy loss:
    </p>
    <div style="background:var(--surface); padding:12px 16px; border-radius:8px; font-family:var(--mono); font-size:12px; color:var(--text); margin-bottom:12px;">
      J(w, b) = - (1 / m) &sum; [ y<sup>(i)</sup> log(&sigma;(z<sup>(i)</sup>)) + (1 - y<sup>(i)</sup>) log(1 - &sigma;(z<sup>(i)</sup>)) ]
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); margin:0;">
      Verified with 200 epochs of batch gradient descent, converging to a test accuracy of 88.52% and ROC-AUC of 0.732.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Feature Schema Table -->
  <div class="card" style="padding:24px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:18px; font-weight:700; margin:0 0 6px;">Feature Schema & Attribute Dictionary</h2>
    <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--muted); margin:0 0 18px;">All 16 features supplied to the preprocessor and model estimators.</p>

